     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and well above the 2,000 mg/day maximum for extended-release. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a more typical dose, titrated up from a lower starting dose in a patient who is new to metformin\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
