       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation alone doesn't change the risk. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I can't find a clinical scenario where that is appropriate. The risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is real, and the order could reach the patient before anyone catches it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter the maximum labeled dose:** metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Enter a different dose** that you specify within labeled limits.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or an attending.** If you think this patient needs an off-label dose, that needs to be a documented decision with pharmacy and attending review. It shouldn't go through me as a routine entry.\n\nIf one of the first two works, tell me which and I'll enter it right away."
